## Linux override for ~/.gitconfig.local (Codespaces / Coder / bare-metal
## Linux). Deployed via .config/mise/config.linux.toml — same platform
## config-file layering mechanism as git/gitconfig.darwin (see that file's
## header for why this isn't a git [includeIf]).
##
## Deliberately empty of a gpg.ssh.program override: these Linux targets
## don't run the 1Password desktop app, so there's no op-ssh-sign binary to
## point at. Git 2.34+ falls back to `ssh-keygen -Y sign` for SSH commit
## signing when gpg.ssh.program is unset, which needs a real private key
## file or an ssh-agent socket available — not verified working in this
## environment; confirm commit signing actually succeeds on a fresh
## Codespace/Coder box before relying on it.
##
## WSL is intentionally NOT covered by this file, even though mise's own
## auto_env platform detection reports WSL as plain "linux" (no separate
## "wsl" platform exists in mise) — see git/gitconfig.wsl for the full
## explanation of why WSL can't be routed here automatically with the
## tools available today.
